// particle_radius picks a milli-unit radius in 0..(import maximum_radius), biased
// toward the center: u is uniform in 0..1000, and squaring it (u*u/1000,
// still 0..1000) compresses the distribution toward 0 -- a uniform variable
// squared has more mass near zero, which is exactly "denser toward the
// core" without needing floats or a real inverse-CDF sample. radius_frac is
// the inverse mapping (radius -> 0..1000 fraction of max), reused by the
// color and thickness falloffs (particles/look/color/pack.id,
// particles/look/position/y.id).

particle_radius(int particle_index) {
  int uniform_sample = random_range(0, 1001 - 1);
  int biased = uniform_sample * uniform_sample / 1000;
  int scaled_radius = biased * (import maximum_radius) / 1000;
} return int scaled_radius;
given initialize_math (0):(450)
given initialize_math (5):(450)

radius_fraction(int radius) {
  int fraction_of_maximum = radius * 1000 / (import maximum_radius);
} return int fraction_of_maximum;
